  L-07 — sitemap hygiene. Two rules, both easy to break:

  1. ONLY indexable pages belong here. `termos.html` and `privacidade.html` carry
     <meta name="robots" content="noindex"> and were listed anyway until Aug 2026 —
     asking a crawler to fetch a page that then tells it to go away. The 404 page is
     out for the same reason. If a page gains a `noindex`, remove it from this file
     in the SAME delivery.
  2. `lastmod` is the date THAT page's content last changed — updated by hand, in the
     delivery that changes the page. It is not a build timestamp and must never be
     bumped globally: a sitemap that claims every page changed today teaches the
     crawler to ignore the field. `git log -1 --format=%ad --date=short -- <file>`
     gives the honest value.

  L-16 — the English version is listed as its own URL. The PT-BR/EN pairing is
  declared by the reciprocal <link rel="alternate" hreflang> tags in each page's
  <head>, which is what Google reads; keeping it out of here keeps this file simple.
-->
